        "selector": {
          "type": "FragmentSelector",
          "value": "xywh=pixel:0,397.81622314453125,4709.7294921875,4690.278015136719",
          "conformsTo": "http://www.w3.org/TR/media-frags/"
        }
      },
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Verso",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>he does not have money.\" This is the talk of an irresponsible person. If possible, please</li>\n<li>meet him and explain to him what is proper. Also, please sue the camel driver for the balance</li>\n<li>and be circumspect and exert yourself to sell what I have sent either for our partnership or on my personal account,</li>\n<li>for, after my arrival in Fustat, I shall stay only a short time, if God wills. You will put me greatly in your debt</li>\n<li>by this and earn my thanks and good prayers.</li>\n<li>And act immediately. A little over twenty bales of paper from a partnership of mine had remained in Tyre.</li>\n<li>I sent them to Ramla, and they have arrived there safely. I also have sent</li>\n<li>fifteen bales from a partnership with you and shall, God willing, carry all the merchandise with me.</li>\n<li>Kindly inform me whether you have received</li>\n<li>a letter from my lord, the elder Ab\u016b l-\u1e24usayn, stating that the rose marmalade</li>\n<li>and the lubricating oil are on my private account. Also, let me know what God has granted you to sell.</li>\n<li>Write me a letter every week, and in Hebrew script, please.</li>\n<li>If you have any order to make, please honor me with it. And may your well-being wax.</li>\n<li>(P.S.) If it is difficult to sell the paper or anything else by weight, and you prefer to sell it at retail,</li>\n<li>do whatever your propitious judgment suggests to you. But, God willing, act without procrastination.</li>\n<li>Kindly inform me, my lord, about the price of Niz\u0101riyya money coined in Damascus,</li>\n<li>for a friend gave me some to sell on my journey. Also the price of the rose marmalade.</li>\n<li>My master Ab\u016b l-Barak\u0101t al-Shar\u0101b\u012b, who has lapis lazuli here in Tyre,</li>\n<li>has five loads of (dried) plums, which find no buyer, in Acre. If plums have a good price (in Fustat),</li>\n<li>write me if he prefers to transport by land, in which case it will cost first 2 (dinars)</li>\n<li>per load from Acre to Ramla by sea and the total price to Fustat will come to 5</li>\n<li>dinars, more or less. Kindly inform me what I shall do in this matter. God alone suffices me.</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 1
    },
